(Item 3's decision: a `buffer` parameter IS the caller's buffer
 (LANGUAGE.md:822), and growth already carries a reallocation back to the
 caller's own cell through `buffer_param_cells` (docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #90).
 `Free` on a parameter rides that exact mechanism - `emit_free_buffer` calls
 `emit_store_back_after_realloc` exactly like `BufferClear`/`BufferResize`
 do - so freeing through the parameter frees the block the caller sees, and
 the caller's own variable ends up naming the shared empty header too.)

a buffer called data is "hello".

To 'release it' with a buffer called b.
    Free b.

'release it' with data.
Print "caller len {data's length}".
Print "caller text [{data as text}]".

append "x" to data.
Print "after append len {data's length}".
